Subject: [PATCH 08567/11362] [outer-loop] Phase 1a: re-derive the 0/296
 world-model wall under the corrected metric

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6233 (openspec/capabilities/arc-world-model-trust-energy/spec.md).

Finding 2 of the ARC live-agent improvement plan: the recorded "0 of 296
clean engine-units reach held-out change_accuracy >= 0.5" wall may be
partly a measurement artifact, since arc_executable_world_model.py:923
documents the metric is dominated by HUD/counter cells rather than real
game state. Three repairs (HUD masking, a symmetric change-fidelity
gate, the REQ-ARC-WMTE-6013 hidden-state branch fix) exist and ship
default OFF; nobody had applied them together to a real corpus.

The original 296-unit corpus's recovery script was never committed and
cannot be re-derived byte-for-byte (confirmed by exhaustive grep + git
log --all --diff-filter=D). scripts/analyze_arc_wall_rederivation_
20260808.py instead aggregates an already-executed, comparable-scope
measurement: experiment_6011_world_model_change_gate_four_arm.json's
four-arm matrix already re-scored 75 real on-disk engines
(arc_e3_origin_fixtures, 25 games x 3 seeds) with mask=1|gate=1 -- HUD
masking ON plus change_gate_decision, the identical function
REQ-ARC-WMTE-6013 wires into the hidden-state branch. No new compute;
a pure re-reading of already-persisted fields.

Result: of 69 eligible (n_changing>=3) engines, 0 pass under the
corrected reading, identical to 0 under the naive reading. HUD masking
measurably narrows near-miss cases (best change_fidelity 0.062 ->
0.145, consistent with the independent 2026-08-01 hud_masked_rescore
finding that masking is real but small) without flipping a single
verdict. The closure hardens.

Honest caveat recorded rather than suppressed: arc_e3_origin_fixtures
is one of the original taxonomy's own provenance-unproven families,
and this corpus's overlap with the original 296 units is unknown. Per
the taxonomy's own reasoning, contamination can only inflate a score,
so this zero is not weakened by the caveat.

Committed with --only: the conductor's own concurrent git-add-A had
staged unrelated files at commit time.

